---
import lake from '../../assets/photos/getting-here.jpg';
import Photo from '../../components/Photo.astro';
import TextSection from '../../components/TextSection.astro';
import { price } from '../../data/facts.ts';
import { linkTo } from '../../data/routes.ts';
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';

const locale = 'en';
---

<Page
  locale={locale}
  page="gettingHere"
  title="Getting here – by train, bus and car to Sils"
  description="How to reach Hotel Lärchenwald: by Rhaetian Railway and bus to Sils/Segl Maria, or by car over the Julier pass or the Maloja pass."
  modified="2026-11-23"
>
  <TextSection>
    <h1>Getting here</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Sils lies in the Upper Engadin, between St. Moritz and the Maloja pass. By train and bus you can reach us easily
      in every season. You will not need a car in the valley.
    </p>
    <Photo
      src={lake}
      alt="Lake Sils with the village of Sils Maria on its shore, and behind it the mountains at the entrance to the Fex valley"
      caption="The view from the hotel across Lake Sils."
    />

    <h2>By train and bus</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Take the Rhaetian Railway via Chur and through the Albula valley to St. Moritz. The line is a UNESCO World
        Heritage Site.
      </li>
      <li>
        In front of St. Moritz station, take the bus towards Maloja. After about twenty minutes, get off at the stop
        “Sils/Segl Maria, Posta”.
      </li>
      <li>
        From the stop it is a five-minute walk: across the village square and up the path into the Fex valley. Our house
        stands at the edge of the forest.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>From the south, the bus from Chiavenna crosses the Maloja pass. It also stops in the village.</p>

    <h2>By car</h2>
    <p>
      From Zurich, drive via Chur and over the Julier pass to Silvaplana, and on to Sils. From Italy, you come over the
      Maloja pass. Both passes are open all year. In winter you need winter tyres, and on some days snow chains too.
    </p>
    <p>
      The centre of Sils Maria is closed to traffic, and only hotel guests may drive up to the house. Your car stays in
      our garage under the house, for {price('parking', locale)} per day.
    </p>

    <h2>Pick-up from the bus stop</h2>
    <p>
      If you have a lot of luggage or there is snow, we will gladly collect you from the stop. Tell us in your request
      which bus you will arrive on.
    </p>
    <p><a class="button" href={linkTo('contact', locale)}>Ask for a pick-up</a></p>
  </TextSection>
</Page>
